A visual event may be observable even when the participant's face is off screen. For each listed interval, check whether a person or their visible body part actually performs or maintains the proposed action. Object-only rest, an automatic machine operation, a title card or a camera movement is not a human event. Return {"checks":[{"id":"given ID","actor_id":"P1, another exact roster ID, local, or none","appearance":"English visible descriptor","evidence":"English visual evidence"}]}. Choose local if a human movement is visible but its identity across shots cannot be established. Choose none if there is no visual evidence of a human actor carrying out this event. Do not assign the presenter to an anonymous hand just because the presenter appears later.
